log-outside 1 0 0
fail-outside 1 0 0
reborrow-raise 1 0 0
log-in-borrow 2 0 0
tick-answering 1 0 0
log-outside-native 0 0 0
fail-outside-native 0 0 0
tick-native 0 0 0
take 2 2 0 # the producer's cell and the count's node; take's answer is one of two closures (the clauses'), called twice
take-all 6 4 0 # the cell and the count's five nodes; take's answer closures, called four times
store-cancel 2 0 0 # the producer's cell and the cell the clause stores κ in
resume-tail 0 0 0
cancel-now 0 0 0
cancel-suppressed 0 0 0
cancel-reraised 0 0 0
loop-tail 0 0 0
loop-captured 0 0 0
recursive-yield 20 0 0 # recursion through a resumption point: one frame object per level, reused at each resume
two-callees 0 3 0 # h is one of two codes that suspend: the call and each resume of its continuation dispatch
two-callees-tail 0 1 0 # the call of h; its operations are direct calls, so nothing is resumed
forward 4 0 0 # the inner clause resumes non-tail while its handler forwards: recursion through the driver and the clause, one frame object each per level
forward-cancel 1 0 0 # the cell, freed by the cancel
multi-shot 0 0 0
